      "id": "EfficientNeuralCodes_NatCommun2022:figure:Fig4:3",
      "kind": "figure",
      "paper_id": "EfficientNeuralCodes_NatCommun2022",
      "label": "Fig4",
      "position_key": "4",
      "position_number": 4,
      "position_suffix": "",
      "page": 3,
      "caption": "Fig. 4 | Schematic of how the learning dynamics of linear networks causes a correspondence between network sensitivity and input statistics. The learning problem is broken into components, each of which learns at a speciﬁc rate. The frequency or variance of a feature of the input data (e.g. the color red) in part determines the learning rate of the components that encode it. This means that the network becomes sensitive to frequent features ﬁrst. Training may end before all features are fully encoded.",
      "caption_en": "Fig. 4 | Schematic of how the learning dynamics of linear networks causes a correspondence between network sensitivity and input statistics. The learning problem is broken into components, each of which learns at a speciﬁc rate. The frequency or variance of a feature of the input data (e.g. the color red) in part determines the learning rate of the components that encode it. This means that the network becomes sensitive to frequent features ﬁrst. Training may end before all features are fully encoded.",
