      "position_number": 1,
      "position_suffix": "",
      "page": 1,
      "caption": "Fig. 1. We explore how the degradation processes affect different frequency components of the image. These observations suggest two critical insights. Firstly, the degradation process, whether due to motion blur, defocus blur, or rain, impacts high frequencies more severely than low frequencies. Secondly, the similarity between high-frequency differences and overall differences highlights the central role of high frequencies in preserving image quality.",
      "caption_en": "Fig. 1. We explore how the degradation processes affect different frequency components of the image. These observations suggest two critical insights. Firstly, the degradation process, whether due to motion blur, defocus blur, or rain, impacts high frequencies more severely than low frequencies. Secondly, the similarity between high-frequency differences and overall differences highlights the central role of high frequencies in preserving image quality.",
