      "position_suffix": "",
      "page": 3,
      "caption": "Fig. 2. (a) The overall architecture of HFP-SAN, which explicitly prioritizes high-frequency components by designing a symmetric encoder-decoder framework whilehandlinglow-frequencycomponentswithasmallerresidualnetwork,therebyproportionallyallocatingcomputationalresourcesbasedontheirrelative importance. (b) Illustration of HFSSA. Instead of applying a dense attention mechanism that computes relationships across all regions and processes every pixel, HFSSA dynamically and selectively focuses on regions with strong mutual correlations in their high-frequency details while avoiding computations in areas with weak correlations or irrelevant black regions.",
      "caption_en": "Fig. 2. (a) The overall architecture of HFP-SAN, which explicitly prioritizes high-frequency components by designing a symmetric encoder-decoder framework whilehandlinglow-frequencycomponentswithasmallerresidualnetwork,therebyproportionallyallocatingcomputationalresourcesbasedontheirrelative importance. (b) Illustration of HFSSA. Instead of applying a dense attention mechanism that computes relationships across all regions and processes every pixel, HFSSA dynamically and selectively focuses on regions with strong mutual correlations in their high-frequency details while avoiding computations in areas with weak correlations or irrelevant black regions.",
